      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(channels): guard ingress queue JSON parse against corrupt DB rows",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\nFixes an issue where a corrupt `payload_json` or `metadata_json` row in the `channel_ingress_events` SQLite table would crash `listPending()` / `listClaims()` with an unhandled `SyntaxError`. A single malformed row makes the entire queue unreadable.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\nAdded a try-catch inside the private `parseJson` helper so corrupt JSON returns `null` instead of throwing. The fix is at the earliest chokepoint — the row parser — so every caller (`baseRecord`, `completedRecord`) is protected without per-call-site try-catch.\r\n\r\nCorrupt rows are still visible in pending lists (with `payload: null`), so operators can detect and remediate them rather than having them silently discarded.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\nA corrupt DB row no longer makes the entire channel ingress queue unreadable. Operators can still see and prune corrupt entries, and the queue continues to serve valid entries.\r\n\r\n## Real behavior proof\r\n\r\n**Behavior addressed:** Corrupt `payload_json` / `metadata_json` in `channel_ingress_events` must not crash `listPending()`.\r\n\r\n**Real environment tested:** Linux 4.19, Node 22, real SQLite DB (not mock), `node --import tsx proof.mts` importing production exports from `src/channels/message/ingress-queue.js`.\r\n\r\n**Evidence after fix (terminal output):**\r\n```\r\n[case 1] createChannelIngressQueue: valid payload enqueue + listPending\r\n  ok: enqueue returns accepted\r\n  ok: pending list has 1 entry\r\n  ok: pending entry payload is correct\r\n[case 2] corrupt payload_json: direct DB insert, then listPending must not crash\r\n  ok: pending list has 2 entries (1 good + 1 corrupt)\r\n  ok: corrupt row is present (not skipped silently)\r\n  ok: corrupt row payload is null instead of crashing\r\n[case 3] corrupt metadata_json: direct DB insert, listPending must not crash\r\n  ok: pending list has 2 entries\r\n  ok: corrupt metadata row is present\r\n  ok: corrupt metadata row metadata is null, not crashing\r\n\r\n=== Summary ===\r\nALL PROOF ASSERTIONS: 9 passed, 0 failed\r\nexit=0\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Negative control — pre-fix behavior reproduced (same script, same environment):**\r\n```\r\n[case 2] corrupt payload_json: direct DB insert, then listPending must not crash\r\nProof script crashed: SyntaxError: Expected property name or '}' in JSON at position 1\r\n    at parseJson (src/channels/message/ingress-queue.ts:222:15)\r\n    at baseRecord (src/channels/message/ingress-queue.ts:233:14)\r\n    at listPending (src/channels/message/ingress-queue.ts:435:30)\r\nexit=1\r\n```\r\nThe corrupt row crashes `listPending()` at `parseJson → baseRecord → map()`, making the entire queue unreadable.\r\n\r\n**Quantified:**\r\n- Fix: 9/9 assertions pass, exit=0\r\n- Main: proof crashes at case 2 with SyntaxError, exit=1\r\n- Vitest: 18 passed (2 new: corrupt payload + corrupt metadata), 0 failed\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n- `pnpm test src/channels/message/ingress-queue.test.ts` — 18 passed, 0 failed\r\n- Standalone proof: `node --import tsx proof.mts` — 9 passed, 0 failed (real SQLite + real queue API)\r\n- Negative control: main crashes at `parseJson → baseRecord → listPending`, exit=1\r\n- No competing open PRs\r\n",
        "branch": "fix/ingress-queue-corrupt-json",
